.TH NIXOS 1 "" "NixOS Flake Helper" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
nixos \- unified wrapper and general command dispatcher for maintaining a NixOS flake

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nixos [command] [args]

.SH DESCRIPTION
A unified wrapper and general command dispatcher for maintaining a NixOS flake.

.SH COMMANDS

.TP
.B apply <test|boot|switch>
.br
Rebuild and apply current configuration.
.br
test   : activate but do not add boot entry
.br
boot   : add boot entry but do not activate
.br
switch : activate and add boot entry

.TP
.B update [inputs...]
.br
Update flake inputs.
.br
If no inputs are specified, all inputs are updated.

.TP
.B clean
.br
Garbage collect old generations.

.TP
.B edit <vars|sops>
.br
Edit variables or sops-nix secrets.
.br
vars : edit variables
.br
sops : edit encrypted secrets using sops

.TP
.B push <host> <path>
.br
Push flake to a remote host via rsync.

.SH DISPATCH
If a command does not match one of the built-in subcommands,
.B nixos
executes it directly inside
.BR $NIXOS_DIR .

This allows convenient interaction with the flake repository:

.nf
nixos git status
nixos cat flake.nix | wl-copy
nixos vi modules/machines/common/firewall.nix
.fi

If no command is passed, the flake directory tree is displayed.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
The wrapper respects the following environment variables:

.TP
.B NIXOS_ROLE
Configuration role.

.TP
.B NIXOS_DIR
Flake path.

.TP
.B NIXOS_SCRIPTS
Commands path.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B $NIXOS_DIR/docs/cli.md
Full documentation.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nixos-rebuild (8),
.BR nix (1)
